```javascript
'use strict';

function createRealmGate(memberships, resources) {
  if (!memberships || typeof memberships !== 'object' || !Array.isArray(resources)) {
    throw new TypeError('invalid gate data');
  }
  const memberCopy = { ...memberships };
  const resourceCopy = resources.map((resource) => ({ ...resource }));

  function realmFor(accountId) {
    return typeof accountId === 'string' && typeof memberCopy[accountId] === 'string'
      ? memberCopy[accountId]
      : null;
  }

  function canAccess(accountId, resourceId) {
    const realm = realmFor(accountId);
    if (realm === null || typeof resourceId !== 'string') return false;
    return resourceCopy.some((resource) => resource.id === resourceId);
  }

  return { realmFor, canAccess };
}

module.exports = { createRealmGate };
```

`memberships` maps account IDs to realm IDs. Every resource must be an object with non-empty string `id` and `realmId`; reject malformed resources with `TypeError`. `realmFor` returns the exact mapped realm string or `null`. `canAccess` returns true only when the resource exists and its `realmId` equals the account's realm. Unknown or malformed IDs return false. Preserve resource order when scanning, accept duplicate resource IDs as distinct entries, and grant access if any matching-ID entry belongs to the account's realm. Construction must copy inputs so later top-level mutations do not alter decisions.

